Hi,

I have the following code and I am trying to use apply
functions to get rid of the for loops, so far I have the following. Any
suggestions about the remaining for loop as this takes a bit long given
that x has around 15000 observations. Thanks.

# original
for (i in 1:length(x)){        # x is a matrix
    for (j in 1:length(x[,1]){
        wx[j] <- max(min(x[j,],up[i]),lb[i])
        wr[j,i] <- wx[j] 
    }
}

# replaced one for loop with apply

wr <- apply(x,2,function(x){
                                 for (i in 1:length(x))  

                                        max(min(x,up[i]),lb[i])
                       })

where up and lb are vectors of length the same as x matrix.

